# Layer 1: CPU mock run (ladder/mock_run.sh). The real orchestration code runs
# end to end; training, model servers, the proposer and nvidia-smi are fakes
# from tests/mock/. Takes minutes, needs no GPU. Never on the laptop.

# 3 cycles x (2 training steps, 2 search iterations x 3 proposals), then the test.
CYCLES=3
STEPS_PER_CYCLE=2
SEARCH_ITERS=2
SEED=7

# Same two-GPU topology as the H100 runs (the fakes report 2 GPUs).
HYBRID_NUM_GPUS=2
HYBRID_TRAIN_BATCH=8
HYBRID_ROLLOUT_N=4
HYBRID_VAL_PUZZLES=4
HYBRID_VAL_ROLLOUT_N=2
HYBRID_EVAL_PUZZLES=16
HYBRID_EVAL_ATTEMPTS=2
HYBRID_TIMEOUT_S=600

# Search: 16 scoring puzzles (the mock data has 16).
LADDER_MH_LIMIT=16
PROPOSALS_PER_ITER=3
PROPOSER_TIMEOUT=120
LADDER_SOLVER_REPLICAS=2

LADDER_GPU_CHECK=skip
LADDER_ALLOW_NO_SLURM=1

# The API rung needs these to start; nothing is sent anywhere.
FIREWORKS_DEEPSEEK_MODEL="mock/deepseek-flash"
FIREWORKS_API_KEY="mock-key"
DEEPSEEK_PRICE_IN_PER_M=0.30
DEEPSEEK_PRICE_CACHED_IN_PER_M=0.03
DEEPSEEK_PRICE_OUT_PER_M=1.20
LADDER_MAX_USD=5
